{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `trans`, `emit`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added top-level protected data variables `trans` and `emit`, computed deterministically from the supplied `z` and `w` exactly as in the original `transformed data` block. Here `trans[k1, k2]` counts transitions from category `k1` to category `k2`, and `emit[k, v]` counts occurrences of word `v` in category `k`. For the supplied data, `trans = [[0, 0], [0, 2]]` and `emit = [[0, 0, 0], [0, 1, 2]]`. Removed the transformed-data construction of these observed sufficient statistics and replaced looped/indexed Dirichlet priors and multinomial likelihoods with vectorized built-in sampling statements on top-level variables, preserving the original product density.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> K; // num categories
  int<lower=1> V; // num words
  int<lower=0> T; // num instances
  array[T] int<lower=1, upper=V> w; // words
  array[T] int<lower=1, upper=K> z; // categories
  array[K, K] int<lower=0> trans; // transition sufficient counts
  array[K, V] int<lower=0> emit; // emission sufficient counts
  vector<lower=0>[K] alpha; // transit prior
  vector<lower=0>[V] beta; // emit prior
}
parameters {
  array[K] simplex[K] theta; // transit probs
  array[K] simplex[V] phi; // emit probs
}
model {
  theta ~ dirichlet(alpha);
  phi ~ dirichlet(beta);

  trans ~ multinomial(theta);
  emit ~ multinomial(phi);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"K":2,"T":3,"V":3,"alpha":[0.20777803527233213,1.2779255102690041],"beta":[4.2537798883297375,0.7235939018963284,1.7952082237533538],"w":[2,3,3],"z":[2,2,2],"trans":[[0,0],[0,2]],"emit":[[0,0,0],[0,1,2]]}","protected_variables":["trans","emit"]}
